From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 17:32:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 240/240] patch 0240 -- #31: independent music/SFX enable
 (4-state)

Generalizes audio enable so music and SFX are independently toggleable --
the engine capability behind SETUP's 'Select Music Card -> No Music' and
'Select Sound FX Device -> No Sound FX' entries. Four states: music+sfx /
music-only / sfx-only / both-off.

Why DOS needs this: previously only AUDIO_OFF (device-level both-off) + the
adlib-specific music-only special case existed. SETUP's Doom-style sound UX
(#32) needs each axis independent on ANY backend. Implemented at the DISPATCH
level, not device-init, because Organya/OGG music ALSO rides the SB mixer that
SFX use -- so they cannot be split at the device:
- _music_off (AUDIO_BACKEND=none OR SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MUSIC_OFF=1) -> music()
  + enableMusic() no-op; the device + mixer still come up so SFX play.
- _sfx_off (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SFX_OFF=1 OR SFX_DEVICE=none) -> playSfx /
  playSfxResampled / stopSfx no-op; music still plays. Generalizes the AdLib
  no-DAC music-only behavior to every backend.
- AUDIO_BACKEND=none gains a selectBackendFromEnv case (No Music; distinct
  from AUDIO_OFF -- the device still opens for SFX).
AUDIO_OFF stays the device-level both-off (back-compat). Resolved once at init;
banner 'Sound system: 4-state audio enable (#31) -- music=.. sfx=..' every boot.

Built clean; default/all-existing backends byte-identical when neither new
flag is set (the gates are no-ops unless explicitly enabled). Full series
re-applies (0239 -> 0240).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
